From a9fb254979fa9e85d637e074526474b399428fe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 10:25:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix and harden Bandit security findings; wire up scan config

Resolve every Bandit finding surfaced by `make security` and make the
scan actually run with a config file.

Scan config:
- Add [tool.bandit] to pyproject.toml. The Makefile already passes
  `-c pyproject.toml`, but no section existed. Exclude vendored/virtual/
  build dirs, the test trees, and dev-only verification scripts (which
  use assert + hardcoded /tmp paths as their test mechanism and are
  never shipped in the wheel).

Real hardening:
- memory_client: reject non-HTTP(S) base URLs at construction, so a
  misconfigured endpoint cannot coerce urllib into opening file:// or
  another unexpected scheme (B310).
- dataset_loader: pin the HuggingFace dataset revision, overridable via
  LEGAL_DATASET_REVISION, so a moving branch cannot silently swap the
  data or loader code underneath us (B615).
- run_logger (src/utils + src/integration) and the Concept_Demos copy:
  replace bare `except:` with specific exceptions so KeyboardInterrupt /
  SystemExit are no longer swallowed (B110).

Documented false positives (inline # nosec + rationale comment):
- B608 SQL: column identifiers come from fixed whitelists/constants;
  every user value is bound via ? placeholders.
- B311 random: non-cryptographic simulation delays and response variety.
- B110/B112: intentional best-effort defensive blocks.

Bandit now reports 0 issues with no warnings. Tests for all touched
modules pass (183 passed); pre-existing failures in test_hebbian_sync
and test_trust_interface are unrelated to these changes.

